            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "awesome in tummy"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This reminded me of a sandwich I had at Disney World but theirs was on a roll with Chicken breast. I used 4 boneless Chiken breast and pounded w/ mallot to flatten. Used 8oz pkg. bacon and par fried in pan,removed and sauteed chicken lightly in grease. Put chicken on large bake sheet, covered w/ cheddar. Then I topped with par cooked bacon,put one pineapple slice on top (small cans have around 4 slices in them.) Then generously sprinkled w/ brown sugar. I baked under broiler until nice and bubbly. Put in a split roll and poured on my favorite bbq sauce. Everyone raved!! Try it this way ,It's more fattening but oh so good!! Thanks Debbie!"
          },
